<text:span text:style-name='caption'><text:span text:style-name='caption-title'><text:a xlink:href='#x1-7001r5' xlink:type='simple'>Figure 5<text:bookmark text:name='x1-7001r5'></text:bookmark></text:a>:    </text:span><text:span text:style-name='textbf'><text:span text:style-name='ecbx-1095'>Fig.</text:span><text:span text:style-name='ecbx-1095'> 5.    Predictability    of    Dominance    direction    reveals    two</text:span>
<text:span text:style-name='ecbx-1095'>mechanistic  regimes.</text:span></text:span>  The  direction  of  Dominance  (which  parental  community  wins)
becomes   increasingly   predictable   from   dominant   species   competition   across   media
conditions,  distinguishing  an  emergent  regime  (Base)  from  a  top-down  regime  (Nutr<!--  l. 107 
