 --><text:p text:style-name='Text-body'> 
<text:span text:style-name='caption'><text:span text:style-name='caption-title'><text:a xlink:href='#x1-8001r6' xlink:type='simple'>Figure 6<text:bookmark text:name='x1-8001r6'></text:bookmark></text:a>:  </text:span><text:span text:style-name='textcolor57'><text:span text:style-name='textbf'><text:span text:style-name='ecbx-1095'>Fig.</text:span><text:span text:style-name='ecbx-1095'> 6.  Dominance  patterns  in  natural  sample-derived  communities.</text:span></text:span>
Natural   sample-derived   communities   show   qualitatively   similar   coalescence   patterns
to    synthetic    communities,    with    Dominance    frequency    increasing    under    higher
nutrient   concentration.</text:span>   <text:span text:style-name='textbf'><text:span text:style-name='ecbx-1095'>a</text:span></text:span>,   Experimental   workflow   follows   Fig. 1c,   but   uses   natural
sample-derived   communities   from   six   environmental   samples   including   soil,   compost,
and   decomposing   organic   matter.   <text:span text:style-name='textbf'><text:span text:style-name='ecbx-1095'>b</text:span></text:span>,   Coalescence   outcome   distributions   in   similarity
space   for   natural   sample-derived   communities   across   three   media   conditions   (<!--  l. 126 
 --><draw:frame draw:name='mobj-198' draw:style-name='mml-inline' draw:z-index='0' text:anchor-type='as-char'><draw:object xlink:actuate='onLoad' xlink:href='./main-m198' xlink:show='embed' xlink:type='simple'></draw:object></draw:frame>
coalescence events per condition, 15 unique pairs <!--  l. 126 
 --><draw:frame draw:name='mobj-199' draw:style-name='mml-inline' draw:z-index='0' text:anchor-type='as-char'><draw:object xlink:actuate='onLoad' xlink:href='./main-m199' xlink:show='embed' xlink:type='simple'></draw:object></draw:frame>
2  replicates).  Similar  to  synthetic  communities,  outcomes  are  more  centered  in  Nutr<!--  l. 126 
 --><draw:frame draw:name='mobj-200' draw:style-name='mml-inline' draw:z-index='0' text:anchor-type='as-char'><draw:object xlink:actuate='onLoad' xlink:href='./main-m200' xlink:show='embed' xlink:type='simple'></draw:object></draw:frame>
and shift toward the axes in Base and Nutr<!--  l. 126 
 --><draw:frame draw:name='mobj-201' draw:style-name='mml-inline' draw:z-index='0' text:anchor-type='as-char'><draw:object xlink:actuate='onLoad' xlink:href='./main-m201' xlink:show='embed' xlink:type='simple'></draw:object></draw:frame>.
<text:span text:style-name='textcolor58'>Gray  points  represent  the  symmetric  counterpart  of  each  coalescence  event  (community
B  versus  A).</text:span>  Histograms  below  show  PDI  distributions.  <text:span text:style-name='textbf'><text:span text:style-name='ecbx-1095'>c</text:span></text:span>,  <text:span text:style-name='textcolor59'>The  fraction  of  Dominance
outcomes  increases  with  nutrient  concentration  in  these  communities</text:span>  (37%  in  Nutr<!--  l. 126 
